course: dictionary
lesson: 415
title: Appreciate: thankful, understanding, or going up in value
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one you need. «I appreciate your help» means you are thankful for it. Swap in a simple word, such as "I am thankful for your help", and see if it fits.
explain: Appreciate can also mean to understand how good or valuable something is and to enjoy it. Someone who stands in front of a painting for a long time may be appreciating its colours. It can also mean to understand a situation fully: «I appreciate it's hard» means you know that it is hard.
explain: With money, appreciate means to go up in value. Its opposite is depreciate, which means to go down in value. Polite phrases such as «I'd appreciate it if…» and «much appreciated» use the thankful sense, so they are useful to learn by heart.
fact: Appreciate is a verb: appreciate, appreciates, appreciated, appreciating.
fact: «Appreciate» can mean to be thankful for something, as in «I appreciate your help».
fact: «Appreciate» can mean to understand how good something is and enjoy it.
fact: «Appreciate» can mean to understand a situation fully, as in «I appreciate it's hard».
fact: With money, «appreciate» means to go up in value, and the opposite is depreciate.
exercise: «I appreciate your help.» What does appreciate mean here? | To lose something on purpose | To count how many people helped | *To be thankful for something | To go up in value
exercise: Maya stood for an hour in front of a painting, looking at every colour. What does she appreciate? | How to paint over it | How heavy the frame is | How much the painting costs in a shop | *How good the painting is, and she enjoys it
exercise: Copy the word that is the opposite of appreciate when money is involved. | valued | appreciated | appreciating | *depreciate
test: «I'd appreciate it if you could close the door.» What does this polite phrase mean? | I would be angry if you closed the door | I would like to paint the door | I would like to count the doors | *I would be grateful if you could close the door
test: «I appreciate it's hard.» What does appreciate mean here? | *To understand a situation fully | To ignore the problem completely | To be thankful for the hardness | To go up in value
exam: Which sentence uses appreciate to mean go up in value? | *«The house began to appreciate in value over the years.» | «Maya appreciated the painting for an hour.» | «We appreciate your kindness every day.» | «I appreciate the cake you baked for me.»
